+/*
+ * ONC (Xiaomi Redmi 7 / onclite, Qualcomm SDM632) internal eMMC root device.
+ *
+ * The eMMC is soldered to the Qualcomm SDCC1 controller: the standard SDHCI
+ * core lives at 0x7824900 ("hc_mem" in the device tree, 0x500 bytes), the
+ * vendor/MCI block that holds HC_MODE and the PWRCTL registers lives at
+ * 0x7824000 ("core_mem", 0x800 bytes), and the applications clock is a GCC
+ * root at 0x1800000.  None of this needs a device tree node: the addresses,
+ * the register sequence and the command/read logic below are the exact
+ * sequence proven from non-secure EL1 on the phone by the shim probe
+ * (xnuios/shim-onc/emmc.c v15, HANDOFF.md section H.13).  That probe
+ * enumerated the soldered eMMC and read its GPT:
+ *
+ *	RCA=1, EXT_CSD SEC_COUNT=0x0747C000 (64 GiB device),
+ *	LBA0 signature 0xAA55, GPT partition names, and 512-byte PIO
+ *	reads of any block (CMD17).
+ *
+ * Four details from that probe matter and are easy to get wrong here:
+ *
+ *  1. The COMMAND register has to be written with a 16-bit store to 0x0e
+ *     (and the transfer mode with a 16-bit store to 0x0c), exactly like
+ *     Linux drivers/mmc/host/sdhci.c does writew(cmd, ioaddr + SDHCI_COMMAND).
+ *     A 32-bit merged store to 0x0c is silently dropped by this controller:
+ *     the command never starts and INT_STATUS stays 0 forever.
+ *  2. The GCC sdcc1_apps root has to be forced on unconditionally
+ *     (CMD_ROOT_EN, bit1) together with the UPDATE latch (bit0).  Left alone
+ *     the root stays parked and the apps branch keeps reading back halted.
+ *  3. HC_MODE and the PWRCTL registers (0x78, 0xdc/0xe0/0xe4/0xe8) are in
+ *     "core_mem" (0x7824000), not at the SDHCI base; only DLL_CONFIG and
+ *     VENDOR_SPEC are at hc_mem + 0x100/0x10c.
+ *  4. 400 kHz identification only needs the always-on XO, so no PLL is
+ *     involved: M=1, N=~3, D=~4 and CFG_RCGR=0x2017 (div 23 = /24, source
+ *     XO, dual-edge MND mode).
+ *
+ * This driver is read-only.  It identifies the card, reads EXT_CSD, walks the
+ * GPT (the header CRC32 is validated so a bogus entry-array location cannot
+ * be trusted silently), prints every non-empty partition, picks one by name
+ * (boot-arg emmcroot=, default "userdata") and exposes it as the BSD disk
+ * "emmcroot0" (block) / "remmcroot0" (character) with 512-byte sectors.
+ * Reads are done with polled PIO, one 512-byte block per CMD17; writes are
+ * refused with EROFS.  Root on it with rd=emmcroot0.
+ *
+ * No interrupt is used and none is enabled: INTEN is held at 0 so the
+ * controller can never raise an IRQ into a kernel that has no handler for it,
+ * and every command polls INT_STATUS instead.  The card stays in 400 kHz
+ * legacy timing / 1-bit bus (no CMD6 HS_TIMING/BUS_WIDTH switch), which is
+ * slow but is exactly what the probe read blocks with.
+ */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+
